# Line endings are part of the build's reproducibility surface: the engine hashes
# snapshots byte-for-byte, and the linters that guard the code producing those
# bytes are byte-sensitive too. Without this, a Windows checkout gets CRLF and
# `gofmt -l` flags every Go file while CI on Linux sees none of it.
#
# `text=auto` lets git detect text and store it as LF; `eol=lf` overrides a
# developer's `core.autocrlf=true` so the working tree gets LF as well.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Research PDFs are already detected as binary, but say so explicitly — a
# mangled sample document would be an obscure extraction failure, not an
# obvious one.
*.pdf binary
